kari: Quick note — our Node quickstart surfaces auth errors as plain Error with message 'permission denied', no status/code. Python shows err.code. Customer sample apps break.

ben: That's bad. Which endpoint?

kari: Embeddings create in hosted, repro in node 16 container.

oscar: Backend sends {code, message, retry_hint} but some edge proxies set content-type so SDK parser falls back to raw text.

ben: Proposal: SDKs must always expose shape {status, code, message, retry_hint, isTransient}. Also publish typed classes (ApiError, AuthError).

docs-elf: I'll add a short onboarding snippet showing robust checks. Example to include:

```js
try {
  await client.embeddings.create({input})
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 'unauthenticated' || err.status === 401) { /* reauth */ }
  else if (err.code === 'permission_denied' || err.status === 403) { /* show perms link */ }
  else if (err.retry_hint === 'retry-after') { /* parse Retry-After */ }
  else if (err.isTransient) { /* backoff retry */ }
}
```

kari: Please include parsing for Retry-After header and a tiny exponential backoff helper.

ben: I'll open a small PR in the node SDK to normalize responses -> ApiError. If body missing, map status->code using canonical map. Add unit tests for flattened proxy responses.

oscar: I'll investigate proxies; if they can't preserve JSON body we'll map on server side before response leaves.

ci-bot: Pinned doc: https://internal.redwood/docs/errors#canonical-shape

kari: Cool. Plan: ben PR + tests (24h), oscar proxy audit, docs snippet (docs-elf). Ping here when PR lands.
